        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Charles Scribner's Sons\n- People: Don DeLillo, Ernest Hemingway, F. Scott Fitzgerald, Kurt Vonnegut, Marjorie Kinnan Rawlings, Stephen King, Robert A. Heinlein, Thomas Wolfe, George Santayana, John Clellon Holmes, Edith Wharton\n- Places: New York City, Scribner Building\n- Topics: Television, nuclear war, sports, language, performance art, the Cold War, mathematics, the digital age, politics, economics, global terrorism\n\nFacts:\n- Don DeLillo was born on November 20, 1936.\n- Don DeLillo is an American novelist, playwright, and essayist.\n- Don DeLillo's works have covered television, nuclear war, sports, language, performance art, the Cold War, mathematics, the digital age, politics, economics, and global terrorism.\n- Charles Scribner's Sons is an American publisher based in New York City.\n- Charles Scribner's Sons is also known as Scribner's or Scribner.\n- Charles Scribner's Sons has published American authors including Ernest Hemingway, F. Scott Fitzgerald, Kurt Vonnegut, Marjorie Kinnan Rawlings, Stephen King, Robert A. Heinlein, Thomas Wolfe, George Santayana, John Clellon Holmes, Don DeLillo, and Edith Wharton.\n- Scribner Building served as the corporate headquarters of Charles Scribner's Sons publishing company.",
